        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Toro's electric lineup is easiest to understand as four tools for four jobs. The Power Shovel handles steps and decks, the corded Power Curve handles a small driveway near an outlet, the 60V single-stage handles the typical paved suburban driveway, and the Power Max e24 handles the wet snow, gravel and plow ridges that used to demand gas.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Pick the class from your snow and your driveway, buy the bigger battery, store it indoors, and the rest of the decision is about which platform's batteries you already own and where the nearest service shop is.
          </p>
